
'''Attributes''' are a set of skills that you unlock after achieving [[Paragon]] Level 1. You can access the Attributes page by clicking the yellow plus sign that appears on the Character portrait, or by clicking the Character portrait and then clicking the table listing Attribute names and values, or by using the Open Attributes ''("O")'' [[Tips, Tricks, and Help|Hotkey]].

==Gaining Attribute Points==

You receive '''Attribute points''' according to a timer, shown in the bottom left of the Attributes page.  The time to gain one Attribute point is

<div style="font-size:150%"><math>\quad\max\left(10,\ 1.25^{\min(50,\ A - 0.2 \times L - 1.75 \times \log_{10} M)} \times 60\right)\ \text{seconds},</math></div>

where
*<math>A</math> = Attribute points already gained from timer
*<math>L</math> = Character level
*<math>M</math> = [[Mysteries]] collected

Attribute points can also be gained through completing some [[Challenges]]. These points do not affect the timer.

Each assigned Attribute point gives a percentage boost, applied multiplicatively.  This yields a total percentage boost of

<div style="font-size:125%"><math>\quad\left(1 + \frac{B}{100%}\right)^X \times 100% - 100%\,,</math></div>

where
* <math>B</math> = Bonus as percentage (e.g. 2.2% for Insight)
* <math>X</math> = Attribute points assigned

Every 25 points assigned to an Attribute grants an additional perk, detailed [[#Attribute Skill Trees|below]].

==Resetting Attribute Points==

Resetting Attribute points refunds all your points, and allows you to spend them again in a different way.  '''You can reset your Attribute points for free upon each Exile''', as long as you mark the "Reset Attributes?" checkbox.

The "Reset" button on the Attributes page also refunds all spent points but costs three [[Nullifier Core]]s, useful only if you need to reassign your points mid-run.

==Item Requirements==

Some [[Items]] have minimum Attribute requirements, and their effects will not be available until these requirements are met.  Using the "Fill" button on the Attributes page will automatically assign free points to meet these requirements.

Note: If an item has Attribute requirements '''and''' grants an Attribute bonus (such as {{ItemTooltip|Legacy}}), the bonus will apply only after the "Fill" button has spent points needed to meet the requirements for all equipped items.  This can cause overspending if that Attribute bonus would help meet the requirements for another item (such as {{ItemTooltip|Ebon Mantle}}).

